  "label": "Racist stereotypes about Black people and water",
  "description": "Harmful stereotypes falsely claiming Black people cannot swim or are afraid of water. These stereotypes ignore historical context (such as segregated pools and beaches) and are used to mock and demean. The presence of Black children in water in this image is exploited to create a racist 'joke' combining water context with the Sea-Monkeys reference.",
